@startuml mfa-multi-step-flow
title VPN MFA authorization (2.2)
actor User
participant "Defguard Client" as Client
participant Edge
participant Core
participant Gateway

User -> Client: click "Connect VPN"
Client -> Client: pick the saved method for each step
Client -> Edge: start MFA (method plan, posture data)
Edge -> Core: pass start request
Core -> Core: check location, device, access and posture
Core -> Core: resolve the user's MFA flow and validate the plan
Core -> Core: start step 1 method and store the in-progress MFA session
Core -> Edge: return session token and step attempt ID
Edge -> Client: pass start response

loop for each step
  Client -> User: ask for the step's proof
  User -> Client: enter code / sign in / touch key / approve on phone
  Client -> Edge: send finish request (token, attempt ID, proof)
  Edge -> Core: pass finish request
  Core -> Core: verify proof
  alt not the last step
    Core -> Edge: step advanced (no pre-shared key)
    Edge -> Client: pass response
    Client -> Edge: start next step
    Edge -> Core: pass step start request
    Core -> Core: start next step method, issue new attempt ID
    Core -> Edge: return attempt ID
    Edge -> Client: pass step start response
  else last step
    Core -> Core: create VPN session and generate pre-shared key
    Core -> Gateway: authorize peer
    Core -> Edge: return completed result with pre-shared key
    Edge -> Client: pass response
  end
end

Client -> Client: configure interface with pre-shared key
Client -> Gateway: establish connection
@enduml
